    ],
    "story": {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "validated-foundation",
          "text": "The work established a bounded foundation before scaling. All eight datasets were present and checksum-valid, with 100 rows apiece across six HUMANUAL splits and two multi-turn SimulatorArena tasks. A one-row-per-task smoke run then passed every split with zero episode errors; the same pass also exposed a strict structured-output requirement, which was tightened and rechecked before the full 800-episode run was submitted.",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-eaf42eaca74c08e0",
              "eventId": "evt-e5837f8ab151d77f69d000ba1ced216889dcadd23f385bdf0cc7e6219805e597",
              "label": "Eight checksum-valid datasets and the planned smoke evaluation"
            },
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-eaf42eaca74c08e0",
              "eventId": "evt-fb3b4437100928f3153143d7af146f07ec60ba9c9f3718a158c8eb0e2a1fe3f9",
              "label": "Smoke evaluation success and structured-schema correction"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "scheduler-failure-and-correction",
          "text": "The first full submission failed at the scheduler boundary rather than in the evaluation itself: Slurm's spooled copy tried to locate the virtual environment under its spool directory. The fault appeared before any API call, so the correction could be isolated to resolving paths from the submission directory and the job could be resubmitted without duplicate or partial evaluation output.",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-e233dacc491b53d7",
              "eventId": "evt-c94ec402851fa51210959fe0c1fbebbbf7b9fd6586875beaa7ff329e34de3b91",
              "label": "Spool-path failure isolated before API execution"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "policy-and-model-waves",
          "text": "The correction became operational policy instead of remaining a one-off fix. A reusable CPU workflow preferred compatible sapphire and seas_compute capacity, required validation before submission, and guarded against duplicate active jobs; preflight availability could still select the immediately usable partition. With that policy in place, the verified runner expanded into isolated, resumable model lanes. Compatibility checks separated models that passed generation and structured judging from Inkling routes blocked by provider policy, preventing deterministic access failures from becoming pointless Slurm jobs.",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-eaf42eaca74c08e0",
              "eventId": "evt-061c097a448c789971595d78d5599265411bfd879efb26771625f0cd6252739b",
              "label": "Reusable CPU-partition policy written"
            },
