          "text": "Later execution problems were handled without erasing their evidence. When real submission RPCs hung despite successful dry-run validation, no job appeared in the queue and no duplicate submission was assumed. A separate smoke lane then revealed that one judge copied a character incorrectly in a long opaque item ID. The exact-ID guard rejected the batch and left it unresolved; shortening judge-visible labels to Q1 through Q7 preserved globally unique internal IDs, allowed only the missing work to resume, and brought that lane to 379 of 379 judgments while the Luna and Gemini lanes remained error-free.",
          "evidence": [
