              "eventId": "evt-62c4c0d95bde2928d1a72fcba741cabc54d90ef7f798c4bb161902dcf57abecd"
            },
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-330c01bc5f17cb0b",
              "eventId": "evt-75f44f6e5abe3234a4b64204b438104bcf5237fc6fdc03d6b76de16c7605205b"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "surface-failures-and-task-reversals",
          "text": "The same diagnostic pass kept operational failures separate from model quality. A partial GPT-5.4-nano run produced 26 structured-grader failures, concentrated in chat and opinion examples, when the judge returned internal or model-like labels instead of the expected candidate labels; these were treated as missing judge outputs, not artificial low scores. SimArena's comparative jobs then finished with 200 of 200 comparisons per judge and zero errors, but the aggregate concealed a task reversal: Claude led the combined result on math, while GLM led decisively on document tasks and Sol was competitive mainly on document interaction style. A final position check found different judges favoring different candidate positions; balanced randomization reduced the risk of reversing the broad order, but it made the close GLM-Claude writing comparison unsuitable for sub-percent interpretation.",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-330c01bc5f17cb0b",
              "eventId": "evt-3bbf4ac9f7db25b9f8b8228b97a44acbf2d936389894f9d5862d08bad0e4083d"
            },
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-330c01bc5f17cb0b",
              "eventId": "evt-6a9846312728e87c240c8351b242b4d88bc31b89db0e7dd790351bc4349f285b"
            },
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-330c01bc5f17cb0b",
              "eventId": "evt-1a6b439e4a02d2c8e1c9b91ba6b63d2374ed482c1d2be9f9315a599fd0e13973"
            },
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-330c01bc5f17cb0b",
              "eventId": "evt-42933feb1b1b785cb4f236bf5c9151fe40f0931798b52fa4cd56f41ccce9e50a"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "compare-judges-on-matched-support",
          "text": "The independent audit introduced another constraint: comparisons had to use matched support. Luna's four-model lane was complete, whereas Gemini had 21 missing judgments, so the analysis used all-four matched subsets for per-dataset score tables—700 targets for Luna and 679 for Gemini—while retaining pair-specific support for win-rate tables. On that basis, both judges chose either GLM or Claude as the best shared model on every dataset and agreed on the dataset winner for six of seven datasets. Because most remaining gaps were small, the report retained support counts and uncertainty instead of presenting the ranks as decisive.",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-19fd7078bb29d827",
              "eventId": "evt-24e1babfac8f4dc31daa84644f67a7e1ac49093a99db722b5949ef867ea65477"
            },
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-19fd7078bb29d827",
              "eventId": "evt-6a88db68bd53ed0dbf96bf1fe0fe1e783bd1d4183f8cc0209b1655207293b97a"
            },
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-19fd7078bb29d827",
              "eventId": "evt-9c94ad9702d4d8f4e2cde46f774ebe472ad6bf683bdbbb6bb39cd3f26ed1a3cd"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "validate-the-evaluators-and-revise-the-claim",
          "text": "The requester then asked whether the original HUMANUAL and SimulatorArena judges, along with a naive baseline, aligned with three evaluators using Kendall's tau, Pearson correlation, and aggregate comparisons. The answer materially narrowed the claim. Against direct-audit references, original HUMANUAL was weak: the three-judge ensemble reached macro tau 0.085, macro r 0.105, pair accuracy 0.567, and target-centered r 0.032. The naive HUMANUAL baseline improved to pair accuracy 0.700 and macro r 0.316 but remained an unreliable substitute. SimulatorArena's style evaluator showed moderate system-level agreement—tau 0.454, r 0.679, and pair accuracy 0.750—yet its audit references agreed weakly with each other on SimArena, limiting any strong validity conclusion. A requested instance-level follow-up changed the emphasis again: original HUMANUAL had a small positive within-model tau across profiles but essentially zero tau for per-instance model-to-model gaps. The final reviewed state was still testing whether removing audit-score ties changed that pair-gap result; the evidence did not yet support a cleaner ending.",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-19fd7078bb29d827",
              "eventId": "evt-8240f74d1d1bfdc1299e71eb7a279eb2bf79b695760f93aa142e848eb3371716"
            },
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-19fd7078bb29d827",
              "eventId": "evt-d0d40e56557303465f32cc8e4361a3af6a6db1e51e9a5edd1dcd8c9669f83fbb"
            },
            {
