        {
          "id": "separate-means-from-winners",
          "text": "Once the reports were comparable, a simple ranking story stopped holding. Under the Luna judge, Claude's mean trailed GLM by only 0.017 and Sol by 0.022, yet Claude won just 25.3% of three-way comparisons; its pairwise rates were 43.4% against Sol and 42.3% against GLM, and it sat within 0.05 of the winner on 54.3% of examples. Luna and Gemini correlated at 0.761 on Claude's numeric scores but selected the same winner on only 49.8% of examples. A distribution check found Claude's scores moving most strongly with GLM at r=0.828, so high scores often improved its mean without producing a distinct first-place result. The analysis therefore favored margin-aware pairwise comparisons with fixed anchors over replacing continuous scores with top-one win rate.",
