      "story": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "evaluator-foundation-lean-runner",
            "text": "The existing API entry still brought in the larger training stack even though the evaluated models were remote. The evaluation agent therefore built a smaller resumable runner around the copied SimulatorArena and HUMANUAL logic, keeping execution and results in a dedicated local workflow. That first runnable design deliberately favored simplicity: the evaluated model filled the simulator, conversational assistant, and judge roles, which established a working baseline but also created the protocol issue that the later role audit had to resolve.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-eaf42eaca74c08e0",
                "eventId": "evt-919e701d152d04c7ecf8d340b20fa2148ef241693bc713223136087841130073"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "evaluator-foundation-reliability-gates",
            "text": "Reliability work quickly became part of the evaluator rather than an afterthought. A missing validator dependency paused one validation path, some free-model routes failed deterministically under provider policy, and one resource shape was rejected during scheduling. The agent responded with bounded generation-and-judge preflights, declined to queue routes that were guaranteed to fail, serialized compatible full runs, and added credential-lane selection that prevented a free-model lane from falling back to the paid credential. Compatible GLM, DeepSeek, and Gemini routes passed the structured preflight; blocked routes remained a provider-access limitation.",
