                "eventId": "evt-b62ea19ce755353670ba61ae53952ac234d274ca013f2fa45d273616d293ccc1"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-eaf42eaca74c08e0",
                "eventId": "evt-f52a7da5f57ca376ec0b44559b1e2ed92ce342d167f6b60e1ef6aca07efdd2e9"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-eaf42eaca74c08e0",
                "eventId": "evt-09df0dc63f6fab12fe94b4217c948dd2a87c4d08d339ef3fb920c2f15ac4a644"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "evaluator-foundation-role-separation",
            "text": "The contributor then tightened the experimental contract: the judge, tutor or writing assistant, and final-document generator should each use a predefined fixed model, completed results should remain intact, and only work that had not started should be cancelled. The agent preserved the running and completed artifacts, removed the unstarted dependency, and implemented three independent auxiliary-model controls. HUMANUAL could reuse an existing target answer and rejudge it, whereas SimulatorArena had to regenerate the conversation because changing the assistant changes the trajectory itself. Inspection of the live configuration and transport confirmed that the role-selected auxiliary model was sent unchanged and was no longer replaced by the target model.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-69088da72373fb09",
                "eventId": "evt-7ca762666a3b083f1faaa68d05c59ca10da32d4a4e1d4e5c528a08c54a1f5535"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-eaf42eaca74c08e0",
                "eventId": "evt-3c09dd3b84fadc87bbb512e11a5151ec6c4a45f64bfde178807f28f1eb77715e"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-eaf42eaca74c08e0",
                "eventId": "evt-69ab93f0dd0f167218c84559b335164c83383ba3f91a3ae9aa7e5d2e8ea425cf"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-e233dacc491b53d7",
                "eventId": "evt-fef2dcdce7f048a71c9e42f0cbe28926fd1d7577be92d7f6bc9efa9be2684b57"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "evaluator-foundation-validated-base",
            "text": "The corrected foundation was validated in stages. Live routing preflights covered both the ordinary interaction path and the separate document generator, and a completed model output could be retained as the source for a fixed-auxiliary HUMANUAL rerun. Later judge-only comparisons finished 200 of 200 items for each judge with zero errors, showing that the reusable routing and persistence paths held under a complete run. The foundation did not erase every external limit: free routes blocked by provider policy still required an access decision, but those failures were now separated from evaluator correctness and no longer consumed full-run submissions.",
            "evidence": [
