[
  {
    "ownerId": "chapter-reporting-and-visualization",
    "chapter": {
      "kind": "handoff",
      "title": "Turning Evaluation Results into a Defensible Presentation",
      "overview": "Evaluation outputs were progressively consolidated into suite-level reports, slide-ready figures, clearer metric definitions, and a final presentation. Revisions to model roles, audit interpretation, statistical claims, and visual layout turned a collection of results into an evidence-bounded narrative about evaluator validity rather than a simple leaderboard.",
      "transition": {
        "before": "The project had completed evaluation artifacts and partial reporting, but no single presentation-ready account of model performance, judge sensitivity, metric limitations, and uncertainty.",
        "after": "The completed local evidence was organized into validated reports, reusable visual assets, and an editable 18-slide deck with a matching PDF, speaker notes, limitations, and appendix support."
      },
      "chips": [
        "Evaluation reporting",
        "Slide-ready figures",
        "Judge sensitivity",
        "HUMANUAL",
        "SimulatorArena",
        "Direct audit",
        "Metric interpretation",
        "Shared-support comparisons",
        "Presentation QA"
      ],
      "people": [
        {
          "id": "research-presenter",
          "releaseLabel": "Research presenter",
          "role": "Evaluation owner and presentation author",
          "description": "Set the reporting scope, requested successive visualization and metric refinements, and defined the final presentation objective.",
          "localIdentityState": "not_identified",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-1200a8ebcfbee55e",
              "eventId": "evt-4d5ca4b685309d7ec7500fe4c01a323767933c60a079baa6c863a033d5b1adef",
              "label": "Initial request for slide-ready evaluation plots"
            },
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-ffc704b32bbfa8ad",
              "eventId": "evt-78740fed313451d3c8ced4b65c984ceb3a3853018ce96151d4791a069cae081a",
              "label": "Request to complete and polish the take-home presentation"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "story": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "reporting-foundation",
            "text": "The reporting layer first had to make the evaluation comparable at the level a reader would actually use. The presenter requested model-wise aggregates for the six HUMANUAL tasks and the two SimulatorArena tasks, followed by inclusion of the completed Gemini run. Gemini contributed a full 800 of 800 records with zero errors. During that reporting work, a code-path comparison also exposed an important validity issue: the local compatibility layer had collapsed the evaluated simulator, counterpart assistant, final-document generator, and default judges onto one model, unlike the original runtime. The report therefore needed to distinguish results affected by role collapse from evidence that remained usable.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-69088da72373fb09",
                "eventId": "evt-8c0b333a00bef499242febced1f1db2148fc96c7831b6ccc3cdcab5c2233c67e",
                "label": "Request for model-by-suite report aggregation"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-69088da72373fb09",
                "eventId": "evt-fc35071656524d85ab9cf9734e09a0bd3c6d29c9dcf95a3989776c84a36a3936",
                "label": "Request to add Gemini Flash"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-69088da72373fb09",
                "eventId": "evt-6832245802d209447d72a8be205b86851d1a2e678eada9b4f098a4cab6845a99",
                "label": "Gemini completion and report regeneration"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-69088da72373fb09",
                "eventId": "evt-a4edcae5d294f2e0198ffe18e9e4ba32a7a5d3c5c9d1d3401937261922c0cc85",
                "label": "Role-collapse mismatch identified"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "first-visual-system",
            "text": "With the reporting foundation in place, the presenter asked for plots that could move directly onto slides while keeping single-model and comparative evaluations distinct. The first delivery produced five 16:9 figures in both PNG and editable SVG, backed by a data snapshot and methodology notes. Follow-up requests added judge-specific rankings, split the SimulatorArena result into separate math and document charts, and expanded the collection with subset-level results rather than forcing every claim into one aggregate view.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-1200a8ebcfbee55e",
                "eventId": "evt-4d5ca4b685309d7ec7500fe4c01a323767933c60a079baa6c863a033d5b1adef",
                "label": "Request for presentation-ready single and comparative plots"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-1200a8ebcfbee55e",
                "eventId": "evt-71a67f31006b754bc32a5bec4fed628215cfe4347e67cdd07c716213eb73767f",
                "label": "First five slide-ready figure exports"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-1200a8ebcfbee55e",
                "eventId": "evt-62adfaa2d3f4eda55e1c8514a9f729269baaff9f7d4a49aba887febcdd8e1400",
                "label": "Request for judge-specific ranks and split SimulatorArena charts"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-1200a8ebcfbee55e",
                "eventId": "evt-e02951f3ffc4b61607b849ff94f958872ef43c3032c0e5eaf52e6c07516cb589",
                "label": "Judge-specific ranking and split-chart delivery"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-1200a8ebcfbee55e",
                "eventId": "evt-e425209e742b5fee1d7d4ae9c8badc9d2c48e01cddb3bf8c08fdc64f0e6d8b1f",
                "label": "Subset-level result and ranking plots"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "scope-and-metric-corrections",
            "text": "The visual collection changed as the distinction between candidate models and evaluators was refined. One regeneration used only GPT-5.4 nano as evaluator; a later correction instead removed Luna and Gemini from the simulator series while retaining them as evaluators, and rebuilt the PNG, SVG, subset, ranking, and documentation outputs. Metric definitions also tightened: SimulatorArena reward was limited to writing- and conversation-style fidelity, with document quality and fulfillment retained only as diagnostics, while fractional win rate explicitly split credit among tied top scores.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-1200a8ebcfbee55e",
                "eventId": "evt-4d75fcd0ca1b0ea9459aa3a3b4159a91c826db360b5324d53daa4a505f0cd9b9",
                "label": "Nano-only evaluator regeneration"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-1200a8ebcfbee55e",
                "eventId": "evt-1f6ef5ce478ab6f0c4da56774fca8a4e86f45b2ed0e2c392220c23d9172e6206",
                "label": "Candidate-versus-evaluator role correction"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-1200a8ebcfbee55e",
                "eventId": "evt-0422a717148c59d0b8180da372c507a08a5b7b77d746559f0ebfd25d6d23b732",
                "label": "Style-only SimulatorArena reward definition"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-1200a8ebcfbee55e",
                "eventId": "evt-77f127e302cce2c831c443bc887994945e704460ad2f857de400a51034c14f6c",
                "label": "Fractional top-score win-rate definition"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "audit-interpretation-becomes-visible",
            "text": "The direct-audit figures forced a more consequential correction in interpretation. Separate D_source, D_specificity, and D_audit charts made their components visible, but inspection of the canonical source-detection answers showed that the absolute-distance transformation treated confident identification of the human and confident selection of the simulator as equally distinguishable. The presentation work therefore preserved direction as well as magnitude: it reported indistinguishability separately from a tie-adjusted simulator-fooling rate, and created stacked distributions by source condition and simulated system. Both judges agreed on the directional model order even where the earlier absolute-distance summary could obscure it.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-1200a8ebcfbee55e",
                "eventId": "evt-9b59b0af20d0c6d4eb6e101629978566346a1f98751a587f425af851ff619818",
                "label": "Separate direct-audit component figures"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-1200a8ebcfbee55e",
                "eventId": "evt-9610c6e8a74b03a39208a27b58465c10a31dbdb367a4865dc17c8f77d948e968",
                "label": "Directional source-score analysis and reporting recommendation"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-1200a8ebcfbee55e",
                "eventId": "evt-00c85a179c1f72ca88ba665fce81aef2c6d5b279160dd473fcb46d9b67b9258a",
                "label": "Source-condition and simulator-system distribution figures"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "from-rank-discrepancy-to-thesis",
            "text": "A remaining discrepancy shaped the presentation's central claim. The presenter observed that Claude could receive comparable absolute scores while winning less often than the other systems and asked for a more nuanced account rather than declaring the evaluation flawed. The analysis found a presentation-position effect: two judges favored the first candidate while another tended toward later positions. Balanced randomization made a complete rank reversal unlikely, but the GLM–Claude writing-style near-tie was not treated as precise to fractions of a point. The direct audit was consequently framed as a lower-assumption diagnostic for whether structured evaluators recover system differences, not as ground truth or an automatic replacement score.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-c4c6af085497b69d",
                "eventId": "evt-82ec93d8134b962665aadcd7f0733a73b59e2825c1d239102e8ec04f3686415e",
                "label": "Request to investigate score-versus-win behavior"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-c4c6af085497b69d",
                "eventId": "evt-6d4f4b462be7ef4aa4bd193a52d745c7a9a8fc2b59594d807fa39c745d31faf5",
                "label": "Presentation-position effect and precision caveat"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-c4c6af085497b69d",
                "eventId": "evt-4d798123dcdc31e11b7d0ea69847731eb62f2bf9a28fec0eefddd7a1261a4b61",
                "label": "Direct audit framed as a diagnostic rather than ground truth"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "deck-design-and-tool-fallback",
            "text": "The final presentation request began with a practical mismatch. The named PDF was the two-page assignment brief, while the attached PowerPoint was the editable 12-slide deck with several placeholder or skeletal slides. No connected PowerPoint session was available, so direct plugin editing was impossible. Focused design questions then fixed the audience, claim strength, shared-support policy, terminology, examples, and deliverables. The resulting specification centered evaluator validity rather than a leaderboard, used only supported model comparisons, disclosed sample size and missingness, led with interpretable audit components, preserved the original files, and targeted 12 core slides plus an appendix.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-ffc704b32bbfa8ad",
                "eventId": "evt-78740fed313451d3c8ced4b65c984ceb3a3853018ce96151d4791a069cae081a",
                "label": "Request to improve and complete the presentation"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-ffc704b32bbfa8ad",
                "eventId": "evt-cbdfff4fbc9e268b38ca004e241d7d969f63df9414983bed9fc2ca2f33e11122",
                "label": "Unavailable connected presentation session and local fallback"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-ffc704b32bbfa8ad",
                "eventId": "evt-95105e9b90b68d76a57bf31524a160de27119f98fa51c9db24bdfb9dc4ceb893",
                "label": "Source-file mismatch and first design decisions"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-ffc704b32bbfa8ad",
                "eventId": "evt-7a428ff26937d1f0986ae428ea4da82570828069eaf394b0980a965ab99840cb",
                "label": "Agreed evidence and presentation specification"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "build-qa-and-handoff",
            "text": "The local build path initially lacked slide-generation and office-export libraries, but a usable toolchain was found and the deck was generated from a shared scene specification so the PowerPoint remained editable and the PDF matched it closely. The first full build contained 18 slides—12 core and six appendix—with notes on every slide and passed structural validation. Visual review still found a legend collision, clipped score and win labels, and tight multiline titles and callouts. Those defects were corrected before both formats were regenerated. The final handoff passed structural and visual QA, matched numeric summaries to local analysis artifacts, paraphrased the two examples, made no new evaluation calls, and left the original brief and deck unchanged.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-ffc704b32bbfa8ad",
                "eventId": "evt-49c687508d5bcdf612127887361fd9ab391196e2fcf1af5d18f9efd7b8d3daac",
                "label": "Missing slide-generation toolchain"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-ffc704b32bbfa8ad",
                "eventId": "evt-195565008794a309ae766f349d4f418381837fdca561b28fd850b8428d60bd5d",
                "label": "Structurally valid first 18-slide build"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-ffc704b32bbfa8ad",
                "eventId": "evt-1c7c050166082d8d93ec86f6a0c9463c78189305a8be792a975f1107ff49e560",
                "label": "Visual defects found during QA"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-ffc704b32bbfa8ad",
                "eventId": "evt-94ef466a164c08103766b6c26fc42d0988dd25cb6da5c6d6774fec36fa9778ee",
                "label": "Corrected build passed final QA"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-ffc704b32bbfa8ad",
                "eventId": "evt-66797110b2bbe9790f63a3b8b457af5afda107e44b40e607f2068e685c6da536",
                "label": "Editable PowerPoint and final PDF handoff"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "uncertainty": "The final deck was complete, but its scientific conclusion remained deliberately bounded: direct audit was presented as a diagnostic rather than ground truth, close rankings were not treated as high-precision differences, and comparisons used completed shared support with missingness and design-dependent composite weights disclosed."
      },
      "insights": [],
      "evidence": {
        "primary": {
          "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-1200a8ebcfbee55e",
          "eventId": "evt-4d5ca4b685309d7ec7500fe4c01a323767933c60a079baa6c863a033d5b1adef",
