            "id": "deck-design-and-tool-fallback",
            "text": "The final presentation request began with a practical mismatch. The named PDF was the two-page assignment brief, while the attached PowerPoint was the editable 12-slide deck with several placeholder or skeletal slides. No connected PowerPoint session was available, so direct plugin editing was impossible. Focused design questions then fixed the audience, claim strength, shared-support policy, terminology, examples, and deliverables. The resulting specification centered evaluator validity rather than a leaderboard, used only supported model comparisons, disclosed sample size and missingness, led with interpretable audit components, preserved the original files, and targeted 12 core slides plus an appendix.",
