          {
            "id": "audit-interpretation-becomes-visible",
            "text": "The direct-audit figures forced a more consequential correction in interpretation. Separate D_source, D_specificity, and D_audit charts made their components visible, but inspection of the canonical source-detection answers showed that the absolute-distance transformation treated confident identification of the human and confident selection of the simulator as equally distinguishable. The presentation work therefore preserved direction as well as magnitude: it reported indistinguishability separately from a tie-adjusted simulator-fooling rate, and created stacked distributions by source condition and simulated system. Both judges agreed on the directional model order even where the earlier absolute-distance summary could obscure it.",
            "evidence": [
