            },
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-f277e3a5243415db",
              "eventId": "evt-44746e763b6661be7467d2a38302c67216f074a71c201da0af712f5b33bdfffb"
            },
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-c4c6af085497b69d",
              "eventId": "evt-77d642c16ce894168a92908675b69ece5292a60998f780454e0d2c3fcdb162ae"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "story": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "local-run-and-reuse-boundary",
            "text": "The requester wanted the evaluation copied into a lightweight local workspace rather than run from the heavy OdysSim tree, then immediately asked whether reusing SOUL data meant the full SOUL codebase had also been reused. The implementation made those questions separable: it prepared an environment with four direct dependencies and fetched only the eight official SOUL test Parquets, with published hashes checked before evaluation. From then on, fidelity claims had to distinguish source data, adapted runner code, and upstream evaluation behavior.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-69088da72373fb09",
                "eventId": "evt-1f2916d807903554193f673d56f263e3eeefcf0511f63c2d904e1b8223a02e5c"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-69088da72373fb09",
                "eventId": "evt-21c1d856cefe1d012c4fb507559ee78e7ee1e180da510a312794ebf77af4b902"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-69088da72373fb09",
                "eventId": "evt-9352800c684385235d932fc52de59657fedcd5f82b6496cd17981d6083122127"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ground-truth-schema-boundary",
            "text": "Schema inspection then established that the two suites did not expose ground truth in the same form. SimulatorArena supplied a sequence of human user turns, while HUMANUAL supplied one held-out human completion; persisted simulator messages also used an internal assistant role and carried wrappers that had to be normalized before shared tokenization. HUMANUAL's stance, emotion, belief, value, goal, and communication dimensions were not six per-example gold labels: the judge inferred alignment on those dimensions from free-text context and the human completion. The resulting metrics therefore depended on explicit adapters and judge behavior, not on a hidden table of six labels.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-330c01bc5f17cb0b",
                "eventId": "evt-8b4cb6d605d833dd34000c5706701465319d738c4405a2bfbcfa2663aebf418d"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-f277e3a5243415db",
                "eventId": "evt-eb18e9a699b2d28f270baaf6e551fa5381c1f05ccae8a69d6f5c57d9fcb27798"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "active-role-and-score-trace",
            "text": "The requester next challenged which model actually acted as the SimulatorArena assistant, whether that behavior came from the original code, and how it affected the score. Tracing the active call graph showed that the evaluated target model played only the simulated user. In the current run, GPT-5.4 nano filled the tutor or writing-assistant role, the judge roles, and the document generator. The active math reward combined writing similarity, interaction similarity, and profile fulfillment equally; the document reward additionally included the final-document rating and separate writing and interaction fulfillment. Several prompt families present in source files—including Turing testing and math correctness—were not called and did not enter those rewards.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-69088da72373fb09",
                "eventId": "evt-2316d4e397a3226946236594d83dbb10fedea82702f51aefd37d1fc9df754387"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-69088da72373fb09",
                "eventId": "evt-f2fd4a0e59db9aee2edb40be94541ed923d1c98433fdd999c17761fdee95dcec"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-f277e3a5243415db",
                "eventId": "evt-44746e763b6661be7467d2a38302c67216f074a71c201da0af712f5b33bdfffb"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "simulatorarena-population-correction",
            "text": "A second provenance challenge corrected the population being evaluated. The local 100 math and 100 document rows were not the original SimulatorArena assistant-benchmark subsets of 50 and 51 conversations. They were SOUL/OdysSim validation samples drawn from the full human-conversation corpora of 450 math and 459 document conversations. All 100 local rows in each task matched the corresponding full upstream corpus, while only 14 math rows and 15 document rows overlapped the smaller benchmark subsets; the local files covered 89 distinct problem IDs and 62 distinct document intents. No released conversion script or selection seed was found, so the exact sampling procedure remained unresolved and the results were labeled as the SOUL/OdysSim adaptation rather than the original assistant benchmark.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-330c01bc5f17cb0b",
                "eventId": "evt-dd0953118c2367a0784fd4a209991ae718c457ee5758d675c06d257067573d6c"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-69088da72373fb09",
                "eventId": "evt-aa5e279e05b057be7a125d022d2956081ef38cf6fd814e2b6cb3f8dc074c1881"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "comparison-protocol-corrections",
            "text": "The same insistence on provenance shaped the later comparative audits. When the requester proposed shuffled, anonymous grading of several HUMANUAL responses, a preflight produced a zero tie and exposed an adapter failure: prompt and completion lived inside `extra_info`, but the comparator had read the top-level row. The run was stopped, the nested-row adapter was fixed, and a regression test was added. The accepted comparison then placed all anonymous candidates in one judge call, kept six dimension scores independent, and split tied wins as `1/k` so win shares summed to one.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-53700865342ab3ac",
                "eventId": "evt-2d39c95de8dd5153ba77f403928bee58faa411da7c42189f00f89c00d5408c35"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-53700865342ab3ac",
                "eventId": "evt-a16a7914baa7bc7651efc4b99240b87c49f80a42fbd953092e8b14c10039bf7c"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-330c01bc5f17cb0b",
                "eventId": "evt-42cb39676f5585a71451eefe6a87ed3520f7c217f0c17ed19036be4d859e97db"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "adaptation-labeled-and-frozen",
            "text": "A proposed Turing-style extension required one final correction: SimulatorArena's original Turing prompts existed in the repository but were not executed by its agents, and they specified a binary conversation choice with confidence rather than the new A-E scale, parser, and reversed-order audit. The new method was therefore described as adapted from that framing, not reproduced from an active upstream metric. When the requester asked what a cleaned HUMANUAL context meant, the agent specified that message text and order would remain intact while identities became stable neutral speaker labels and dataset IDs, model names, system instructions, wrappers, and the held-out completion were excluded. Tests then verified opaque item IDs, orientation recoding, and deterministic randomization before a 700-target manifest was frozen from existing history pools without resampling profiles. The final boundary was explicit: the evaluation could be reproducible and auditable without claiming that every local mechanism was original or that the unreleased SOUL sampling procedure was known.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-c4c6af085497b69d",
                "eventId": "evt-77d642c16ce894168a92908675b69ece5292a60998f780454e0d2c3fcdb162ae"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-c4c6af085497b69d",
                "eventId": "evt-03f5bd5d94c8b68915b2f150a6e59becb7faaddc7a39c3780314e62738e0d987"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-c4c6af085497b69d",
                "eventId": "evt-552ba6d0b9129b3554122b7a545462e25b05e8fe7cf2d5adcedc1b8aef656008"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-c4c6af085497b69d",
                "eventId": "evt-c64d887a8518ecad44a010553a51b7a78a33eef4a36d2c7a1c13d051b282c542"
              },
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-c4c6af085497b69d",
                "eventId": "evt-2dc69953485b9d1512d99a83143988faa7644a5b45ddf6a1e471a71a2bf6fb80"
              }
            ]
          }
