                "eventId": "evt-9352800c684385235d932fc52de59657fedcd5f82b6496cd17981d6083122127"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ground-truth-schema-boundary",
            "text": "Schema inspection then established that the two suites did not expose ground truth in the same form. SimulatorArena supplied a sequence of human user turns, while HUMANUAL supplied one held-out human completion; persisted simulator messages also used an internal assistant role and carried wrappers that had to be normalized before shared tokenization. HUMANUAL's stance, emotion, belief, value, goal, and communication dimensions were not six per-example gold labels: the judge inferred alignment on those dimensions from free-text context and the human completion. The resulting metrics therefore depended on explicit adapters and judge behavior, not on a hidden table of six labels.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-330c01bc5f17cb0b",
                "eventId": "evt-8b4cb6d605d833dd34000c5706701465319d738c4405a2bfbcfa2663aebf418d"
