        "localIdentityState": "not_identified",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-c4c6af085497b69d",
            "eventId": "evt-08988bbd0bc7fa8f6d15044f0534a804ce153c074be8d282159d4e0911693ce4"
          },
          {
            "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-c4c6af085497b69d",
            "eventId": "evt-ce810e270bc5eb36bfbd102e815c0346bdb931c559336a0f92f83af508a0170b"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "audit-implementation-agent",
        "releaseLabel": "Audit implementation agent",
        "role": "Judge-only comparison and direct-audit validation",
        "description": "Reconstructed fixed conversations for judging, implemented the anonymous comparators, validated reversal and leak checks, and formalized the full audit's score orientation.",
        "localIdentityState": "not_identified",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-c4c6af085497b69d",
            "eventId": "evt-388539cd82d2cebe2d31a253d81bcc2d214c1ae90c6d519c4bcb59cdcf5b2d81"
          },
          {
            "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-c4c6af085497b69d",
            "eventId": "evt-1286aa99c509540e703e89a6164f613da6df558317178f8f736a4e6bfa26ee1a"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "story": {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "freeze-trajectories-before-comparing-judges",
          "text": "The comparative method first fixed what could change. For SimulatorArena, every Sol, GLM, and Claude source contained 100 math and 100 document trajectories generated with the same GPT-5.4-nano auxiliary assistant, including the document generator where applicable. Because stored roles were written from the simulator's perspective, the judge-only loader reconstructed the public conversation rather than replaying the evaluator and regenerating the role play. The resulting comparator used deterministic anonymous shuffling, separate writing and interaction scores, combined and pairwise summaries, fractional win rates, task-level views, and trajectory hashes, while explicitly rejecting sources that did not use the fixed assistant.",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-c4c6af085497b69d",
              "eventId": "evt-594197f1f8772d2792dbd6ab5d394cf38c59cafd7c28e0cf3b6e60a784645f7c"
            },
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-c4c6af085497b69d",
              "eventId": "evt-388539cd82d2cebe2d31a253d81bcc2d214c1ae90c6d519c4bcb59cdcf5b2d81"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "make-humanual-comparisons-anonymous-and-auditable",
          "text": "HUMANUAL used a related but task-specific design. One judge call received the Sol, GLM, and Claude responses in a deterministic random order with no model identities, then scored each candidate independently on stance, emotion, belief, value, goal, and communication before the existing length factor was applied. Tied maxima split one win as 1/k, making the three fractional win rates sum to one; outright wins, means, candidate positions, and pairwise rates were retained rather than collapsed into a single ranking. That distinction mattered because mean similarity and top-one frequency answer different questions and can order the same candidates differently.",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-eaf42eaca74c08e0",
              "eventId": "evt-66702204a46ee26e3e2e12bf45e4c41666365849aa114fe47b1d18ad2b21b6a5"
            },
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-eaf42eaca74c08e0",
              "eventId": "evt-01a9c806f1377e8f49ac7969e8994812e216173244d40271a37c4e2b3c860ef7"
            },
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-c4c6af085497b69d",
              "eventId": "evt-727a29d6dc0c2e4d0a6080fc3d66017e38c87b18245826576b66287b7861e5a6"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "let-preflight-failure-correct-the-adapter",
          "text": "A preflight prevented a silent validity failure. An apparent zero tie was not judge behavior: the comparator had read the top-level parquet row even though HUMANUAL stored its prompt and completion inside `extra_info`, so the new judges received an empty ground truth. The implementation agent corrected the adapter, added a regression test for nested rows, and reran all three preflights into a fresh directory before any full comparison was submitted.",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-eaf42eaca74c08e0",
              "eventId": "evt-8496b3f8ef22dc7f60e8d60b6eb043fa744125a545430623cb341a8d107b9f78"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "turn-the-proxy-check-into-a-controlled-direct-audit",
          "text": "The requester narrowed the next comparison to diagnostic validation, independent judge replications, and per-user pairwise system agreement. HUMANUAL chat was excluded because it differed from the other subsets. To avoid revealing what was being graded, evaluators would choose an anonymous A–E category ranging from favoring the first response, through indistinguishable, to favoring the second; presentation order would be reversed in the pilot, histories and profiles would remain fixed, and numeric conversion would happen afterward. For SimulatorArena, the audit reused the original Turing-test structure but supplied only cleaned, ordered user messages—excluding assistant text, identifiers, model names, system prompts, and source metadata.",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-c4c6af085497b69d",
              "eventId": "evt-08988bbd0bc7fa8f6d15044f0534a804ce153c074be8d282159d4e0911693ce4"
            },
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-c4c6af085497b69d",
              "eventId": "evt-ce810e270bc5eb36bfbd102e815c0346bdb931c559336a0f92f83af508a0170b"
            },
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-c4c6af085497b69d",
              "eventId": "evt-c780cb3d4dae54e80a75aeda17338b5a2dc95703a1ba5635340b0fc47c376bde"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "use-the-smoke-test-to-bound-the-claim",
          "text": "The pilot was deliberately small: one fixed target from each of seven datasets produced 379 logical judgments per evaluator, including 182 forward-and-reversed pairs. Every direct-audit lane completed 379 of 379, all reversal pairs were present, no model or agent identities leaked through the prompts, and separate SimulatorArena absolute rejudgments completed six of six per judge. The smoke run nevertheless exposed substantial judge and order sensitivity. One Nano lane also stopped after 344 judgments because long opaque identifiers were copied incorrectly; a recovery lane finished the remaining 35 with short batch-local identifiers. Those results were therefore labeled smoke-test observations rather than conclusions.",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-c4c6af085497b69d",
              "eventId": "evt-9c8a9500ec1c4365447dd0aeb089db5b6e6f9dfeb9f8a5b8cfff8916a8f52789"
            },
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-c4c6af085497b69d",
              "eventId": "evt-7793fb7769b752d66097dc98d6d98935a1ef8a311f338842b8803d885016a77e"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "scale-with-explicit-orientation-and-matched-instance-tests",
          "text": "The full design expanded to all 100 rows in each of seven datasets, used two fixed comparison histories per dataset, and reduced each item to one deterministic randomized order rather than repeating both orders. Real-versus-simulated choices were recoded so higher signed scores always favored the simulator, independent of presentation order. Distinguishability distances measured how far the judgment sat from indistinguishable, and the combined audit weighted specificity by one half and history-aware and context-only source detection by one quarter each. Because absolute distance gives the same penalty when a judge confidently identifies the human and when it confidently mistakes the simulator for human, signed diagnostics were retained and reported separately. Downstream Kendall tau-b validation used matched instances, preserved ties, reversed the audit sign because lower distance was better, averaged simulator-specific and pair-gap correlations within each dataset, and weighted datasets equally instead of correlating only three model means.",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-c4c6af085497b69d",
              "eventId": "evt-8ef021248c36afb975c9686d3b06848015cc572d16e69e2cb326c42ae59da917"
            },
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-c4c6af085497b69d",
              "eventId": "evt-1286aa99c509540e703e89a6164f613da6df558317178f8f736a4e6bfa26ee1a"
            },
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-c4c6af085497b69d",
              "eventId": "evt-3503596d83b33866f3ca5401ab3b00e1c7bf163f48c5375f89e049991dcf0864"
            },
            {
              "documentId": "traj-zxiong-codex-19fd7078bb29d827",
              "eventId": "evt-fcd6be6d0772bb03db6dc0d26eb95ce009b204578e9ba66707fd17f3aa6f4dbb"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "uncertainty": "The combined direct-audit distance measures distinguishability, not whether the judge selected the real source in the correct direction. Signed diagnostics reduce that ambiguity but remain a separate reported quantity rather than changing the distance formula."
    },
